   "h1": "What Is Line Clearance? Definition & Steps",
   "lead": "Line clearance is the check that a production line is free of previous product, labels and documents before the next batch. Steps, example, digital tips.",
   "answer": "Line clearance is the documented check that a production or packaging line is free of materials, labels and documents from the previous batch before a new batch starts. It prevents mix-ups. It is critical in pharma and food. Actarion makes line clearance a guided digital checklist with photo proof.",
